<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE policyconfig PUBLIC
 "-//freedesktop//DTD PolicyKit Policy Configuration 1.0//EN"
 "http://www.freedesktop.org/standards/PolicyKit/1/policyconfig.dtd">
<!--
  /usr/share/polkit-1/actions/com.mrog.lease.policy
  FLEET-CB2 2026-09-05.

  Lets the notch dot raise polkit's OWN password dialog to arm an agent root
  lease.

  ==========================================================================
  FIXED 2026-09-05 from the Omarchy desktop. TWO bugs, one of them serious.

  BUG 1, THE SERIOUS ONE: this file was NOT VALID XML, and polkit was
  silently dropping the whole action. A comment line carried a DOUBLE HYPHEN,
  which XML forbids inside a comment. The offending line was the one
  describing why remote sessions are refused; the two dashes it used as
  punctuation are what broke it.

  This failed silently in the worst way. The file was present, correct
  looking, and readable, and everything about it invited the conclusion that
  it was in force. It was not. On mrog, listing polkit actions showed
  com.mrog.legal.toggle and did NOT show com.mrog.lease.grant.

  What happened instead: with the action unregistered, pkexec falls back to
  org.freedesktop.policykit.exec, whose defaults allow BOTH any and inactive
  sessions subject to an admin password. So the rule this file exists to
  state, that the gate must never be reachable from a remote or switched away
  session, was not merely absent. The fallback permits precisely that.

  NOTE FOR WHOEVER EDITS THIS NEXT: no double hyphen may appear anywhere in
  this comment, including inside example commands. Validate the file before
  trusting it; presence on disk proves nothing, as the last four hours show.

  BUG 2: allow_active was auth_admin_keep. The keep was deliberate, reasoned
  as covering a mis-click. It does, but it also covers an AGENT. An agent can
  invoke pkexec too, and inside polkit's keep window a grant is authorised
  SILENTLY, with no dialog and no chance for Chris to see it, turning the
  approval gate into one click then free for the rest of the window. It is
  now auth_admin with no keep. The cost is a password on every grant,
  including after a mis-click. That is the correct price for a capability an
  agent is allowed to ask for.
  ==========================================================================

  allow_any and allow_inactive are both no on purpose. This must only be
  reachable from a real, active, local session, never from a remote or
  switched away one.
-->
<policyconfig>
  <vendor>mrog</vendor>
  <vendor_url>https://localhost</vendor_url>

  <action id="com.mrog.lease.grant">
    <description>Arm an agent root lease</description>
    <message>Authentication is required to give an agent temporary root on this machine.</message>
    <icon_name>dialog-password</icon_name>
    <defaults>
      <allow_any>no</allow_any>
      <allow_inactive>no</allow_inactive>
      <allow_active>auth_admin</allow_active>
    </defaults>
    <annotate key="org.freedesktop.policykit.exec.path">/usr/local/sbin/mrog-lease-ui</annotate>
    <annotate key="org.freedesktop.policykit.exec.allow_gui">true</annotate>
  </action>
</policyconfig>
